{"name":"Zodiac","hex":"#8b9196","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Zodiac","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of zodiac."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Zodiac Killer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Zodiac"}],"entries":[{"title":"Zodiac","blocks":[{"text":"The zodiac is a belt-shaped region of the sky that extends approximately 8° north and south celestial latitude of the ecliptic – the apparent path of the Sun across the celestial sphere over the course of the year. Within this zodiac belt appear the Moon and the brightest planets, along their orbital planes. The zodiac is divided along the ecliptic into 12 equal parts, called \"signs\", each occupying 30° of celestial longitude. These signs roughly correspond to the astronomical constellations with the following modern names: Aries, Taurus, Gemini, Cancer, Leo, Virgo, Libra, Scorpio, Sagittarius, Capricorn, Aquarius, and Pisces."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Ecliptic_path.jpg/330px-Ecliptic_path.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zodiac"},{"title":"Zodiac (comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Zodiac is the name of several groups of fictional characters appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4c/Zodiac-comics.gif/330px-Zodiac-comics.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zodiac_(comics)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Zodiac_Constellations.jpg/500px-Zodiac_Constellations.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Zodiac_Constellations.jpg/500px-Zodiac_Constellations.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_c